DevOps Interview Command Series — Terraform (Day 11) 🌍

Terraform is the backbone of Infrastructure as Code (IaC).
It enables DevOps teams to provision, version, and manage cloud infrastructure safely and repeatedly.

If you’re preparing for DevOps / SRE / Cloud interviews, these are the Terraform commands you must know:

terraform --version
terraform init
terraform init -upgrade

terraform validate
terraform fmt
terraform fmt -recursive

terraform plan
terraform plan -out=tfplan

terraform apply
terraform apply tfplan
terraform apply -auto-approve

terraform destroy
terraform destroy -auto-approve

terraform show
terraform state list
terraform state show resource_name

terraform output
terraform refresh

terraform workspace list
terraform workspace new dev
terraform workspace select prod

🎯 Interview Focus
• What is IaC and why Terraform?
• terraform init vs plan vs apply
• State file importance & locking
• Remote backend & state security
• Workspaces vs environments
• Handling drift & rollback scenarios
• Terraform vs Cloud-native templates
